  push(H2('8.4  Coda'));
  push(P0(`The ground, then, is this. A construction of the corpus's kind, as its manuscripts state it, delivers a limit that is controlled at short distances and silent at long ones: a theory whose correlations obey the axioms of positivity and symmetry, whose coupling is seen to run, and whose large-distance behaviour is not controlled. Theorem 7.1 shows that the missing control is a single spectral fact. Theorem 7.4 shows that this fact is a property of the rungs: an inequality on the lattice, where reflection positivity has made a quantum mechanics of the theory before any limit is taken. The proof that follows takes up that inequality on that sequence.`));
